<launch>
  <!-- LEO Rover — static TF gaps that MINS needs and nothing currently publishes.

       WHAT ALREADY EXISTS (do NOT redefine these here, they'd conflict):
         - base_link, odom, imu_frame, and the wheel joints are published by
           robot_state_publisher from leo.urdf.xacro (started in
           leo_bringup.launch on the robot). imu_frame is the STOCK onboard
           IMU on the LEO Rover mainboard, wired to firmware_message_converter
           (imu_frame_id: imu_frame, leo_bringup/config/firmware_message_converter.yaml).
         - camera_link, camera_infra1_optical_frame, camera_infra2_optical_frame,
           camera_gyro/accel_optical_frame etc. are self-published by the D455's
           own realsense2_camera node the moment it starts (its internal tree is
           complete and correct on its own — it just isn't attached to base_link).

       WHAT'S MISSING (this file adds it):
         - base_link -> camera_link : the D455 was bolted on aftermarket
           (upgrade from the stock RaspiCam), so the stock xacro has no idea
           it exists. Nothing currently ties the D455's self-published tree
           into the chassis tree.
         - base_link -> laser : same story for the RPLidar (see
           VINS_to_MINS_Test_Plan.md Tier 3.2 — this was already flagged as
           unmeasured there).

       VALUES BELOW ARE PLACEHOLDERS — replace with real numbers before
       trusting MINS output:
         1) Tape-measure now (fastest unblock): x/y/z in meters from base_link
            origin, roll/pitch/yaw in radians.
         2) Better, once kalibr_calibrate_imu_camera finishes (this session's
            other in-progress task) and produces T_cam_imu: compose it with
            the URDF's own base_link->imu_frame static transform instead of
            re-measuring by hand —
              T_base_camera = T_base_imu (from the URDF, already exact)
                              * inverse(T_cam_imu)  (from Kalibr, once available)
            which is more accurate than a tape measure for the same effort.
  -->

  <!-- base_link -> camera_link (PLACEHOLDER: measure or derive, see above) -->
  <node pkg="tf2_ros" type="static_transform_publisher" name="base_to_camera"
        args="0.15 0.0 0.10  0 0 0  base_link camera_link"/>
  <!-- args: x y z  yaw pitch roll  parent  child -->

  <!-- base_to_laser SUPPRIMÉ (audit 2026-07-08) : l'URDF publie déjà la
       chaîne base_link->rplidar_link->laser_frame — deux chaînes TF pour le
       même capteur étaient redondantes. Au bring-up RPLidar : mesurer et
       renseigner la chaîne URDF existante, pas celle-ci. -->
</launch>
